{
  "$comment": "Expression's declarations (lib/expression.js). Languages are a registry: each names its script and writing direction, so a right-to-left language lays out right to left with no code. The storefront's shipped copy (lib/seed/settings.json copy) is written in sourceLanguage; a catalogue holds the same keys in another language, as rows of the message catalogue (the messages table), editable in the console. A request is answered in the shopper's chosen language, else the best one their browser asks for, else the language of the store's locale, else sourceLanguage — always one that has a catalogue or is the source. A {placeholder} is kept as written. A store's own saved copy overrides the catalogue in its own language only.",
